A||N||1||Bob Englert||Exhaust gasket on Duke ?||||5||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||08-07-2001||05:47 PM||||I am in the process of replacing the head gasket on my daughter's 87 coupe (the one that didn't make it to Williamsburg).  I noticed that the exhaust gasket that came out of the car looked like a composite type while the gasket in the set I got from CarQuest was a shiny metal one.<P>I also discovered that the gasket was between the exhaust manifold and the heat shield but there was not any gasket between the head and heat shield, only Permatex Ultra Copper material.<P>Should there be a gasket on both sides of the heat shield?  Is the shiny metal gasket the right one or should I look for a different gasket style?<P>The head is getting checked out at the machine shop and I should have it back by the weekend.  Hopefully we will have the car back on the road sometime next week.<P>Thanks for any advice....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-07-2001||06:52 PM||||Head &gt; Shield &gt; Gasket &gt; Manifold<P>don't forget to put antisieze on the bolts.<P>the metal gasket is fine.<P>torque the bolts to spec in the order shown in the haynes book.||||reg||1
